        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-17T22:25:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android already implements a mechanism to reclaim background processes using process_madvise(): https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/services/core/jni/com_android_server_am_CachedAppOptimizer.cpp. Why is that not enough?",
      "parentUuid": "9bd4f4b1_544db7ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4405,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "188a460740bbaad4b6a47de84fa456e8acf767e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94e40a6f_caf1ac70",
        "filename": "mm/vmscan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4405,
      "author": {
        "id": 3616462
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T01:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. There is an mm lock contention issue with process_madvise(). When the app switches to the background while process_madvise is executing, and then switches back to the foreground, there will be a 1-second stutter.\n2. Android reclaims background processes only when the app switches to the cache state. We need to implement freezing and partial compression when the app is not in the foreground, and full compression when the app has been in the background for a long time.\n3. Compression based on memcg is simpler to implement than compression based on processes.",
      "parentUuid": "9c97247a_76889207",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4405,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "188a460740bbaad4b6a47de84fa456e8acf767e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c69809d6_7592d269",
        "filename": "mm/vmscan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T19:22:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. So, I\u0027m guessing you are implementing something like partial MADV_PAGEOUT. And you would still need to hold the mmap_lock, just for a shorter amount of time?\n\nWouldn\u0027t it be easier to export `do_madvise()` instead and add a hook inside `madvise_cold_or_pageout_pte_range()` to terminate the loop earlier to limit the number of isolated pages and then reclaim them? That seems like a more straight-forward and ribust approach than exporting individual internal functions.",
      "parentUuid": "94e40a6f_caf1ac70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4405,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "188a460740bbaad4b6a47de84fa456e8acf767e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "165675fc_fd4e18c9",
        "filename": "mm/vmscan.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4405,
      "author": {
        "id": 3616462
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T12:27:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using do_madvise is process-based for memory reclamation. Therefore, if we want to reclaim memory for an app, we need to traverse multiple processes. However, we utilize the per-app memory control group (memcg) feature, which allows us to reclaim memory for an app based on a single memcg. This approach simplifies the code implementation and makes it more efficient.\nmemcg-\u003elruvec-\u003elrugen-\u003efolios[gen][LRU_GEN_ANON][zone];",
      "parentUuid": "c69809d6_7592d269",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4405,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "188a460740bbaad4b6a47de84fa456e8acf767e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
